<Guide
  title="Local SEO for HVAC, Plumbing & Roofing Companies in DFW — Azoth & Co."
  description="How home service businesses in Dallas–Fort Worth win the Google map, the top results and AI answers across a service area. The fixes that matter for HVAC, plumbing, roofing and electrical."
  label="Home services"
  heading="Local SEO for home service businesses in DFW."
  sub="HVAC, plumbing, roofing, electrical. The customer with a broken AC in July calls one of the first three names. Here is how to be one of them."
  published="2026-11-11"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p>
    Home service searches are urgent. A homeowner with water on the floor in Prosper or a dead AC in Denton is not
    comparing ten websites. She calls one of the first names she sees on the map, or the one an AI assistant suggests.
    Being fourth is close to being invisible.
  </p>
  <p>
    Trades have one problem a storefront does not: you serve an area, not an address. Here is how that changes the work.
  </p>

  <h2>Win the map across a service area</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Set up as a service-area business.</strong> Hide the address if customers do not come to you, and list the cities you actually cover.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose the exact primary category.</strong> “HVAC contractor”, “Plumber”, “Roofing contractor”, “Electrician”. Add secondary categories only for work you really do.</li>
    <li><strong>List every service.</strong> AC repair, furnace installation, water heater replacement, drain cleaning, roof inspection. Customers and Google both match on these.</li>
    <li><strong>Know where you rank, town by town.</strong> Map rankings change by distance. You may be first in your own town and invisible twenty minutes away. Grid tracking shows exactly where.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Build the pages that carry you further out</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>One page per service.</strong> What the job involves, signs you need it, how it is priced, how fast you come out.</li>
    <li><strong>Real area pages, not copies.</strong> Write about the towns where you do the most work: jobs done there, common problems, how quickly you reach them. Skip the pages you cannot make genuinely different.</li>
    <li><strong>Emergency and seasonal pages.</strong> “Emergency plumber”, “AC not cooling”, “hail damage roof inspection” are searched hard at specific times. Have the page ready before the season.</li>
    <li><strong>Fast on a phone, number at the top.</strong> Most of these searches happen on a phone, often in a hurry. One tap to call.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reviews that name the job and the town</h2>
  <p>
    Ask at the end of every job, with a direct link texted before the truck leaves. Reviews that mention the service and
    the town help both customers and rankings. Reply to every one. Never pay or offer anything for a review.
  </p>

  <h2>Show up in AI answers</h2>
  <p>
    Homeowners increasingly ask ChatGPT or read Google’s AI answer before they call. Assistants recommend companies they
    can confirm across sources: your profile, your site, reviews, directories like the BBB and your trade’s own
    listings, and supplier dealer pages. Read <a href="/visibility/ai-search/">how AI search chooses</a> for the full list.
  </p>

  <h2>What the Visibility Audit covers for a trade</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Map rankings for your top services across your whole service area</li>
    <li>Your profile against the three companies that show up instead of you</li>
    <li>Service and area pages, mobile speed and call flow</li>
    <li>What AI assistants say when a homeowner asks for your trade in your towns</li>
    <li>A ranked fix list with 90-day targets</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We take one company per trade per town. The first to book gets the work. <a href="/visibility/#audit">Start with the
    Audit</a>, or check yourself first with the free <a href="/visibility/scorecard/">Scorecard</a>.
  </p>
</Guide>
